        <h2>A claim about a book is not a warrant against a neighbor.</h2>
        <p>This page rejects a public claim: that Muhammad is the prophet Deuteronomy 18 announced, and that the Torah and the Gospel write him. The claim is in Quran 7:157. The test is in the chapter the claim has to survive. He does not survive it, if the Meccan report is history. If the report is not history, the chapter was never theirs to wave.</p>
<p>Nobody on this page is sentenced. Deuteronomy’s death penalty is quoted because it is the verse, not because a website inherits a Bronze Age court. Private prayer is not the target. The target is the announcement.</p>
<p>The deduction in its published Christian form is David Wood’s, under the title “Two Simple Proofs that Muhammad Was a False Prophet.” The documents are older than either of us: Deuteronomy, the Quran, al-Tabari, al-Bukhari. islamophobe.me argues the legal system built on the claim. The food pages argue the jurisdiction at the table. This page stays on the prophet.</p>
