        <h2>Muhammad does not pass the verse used to announce him. A prophet who spoke for other gods, or who spoke for God what God had not said, is the false prophet of Deuteronomy 18:20.</h2>
        <div class="prose"><p>That is a conclusion inside a text, on a report the text’s later guardians tried to bury. It is not a mood, and it is not a riot.</p>
<p>Keep the report, and the classification follows. Burn the report, and the Torah citation in Quran 7:157 loses the only passage they were willing to read aloud. There is no third door in which Deuteronomy announces him and refuses to judge him.</p>
<p>This page does not call for harm to any person. It calls the claim false.</p></div>
